WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.574
"Hey, sweet little bear.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.409
Do you like being tickled?"

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.277
Bears can be cute.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.679
But for most people,

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.416
bear encounters aren't
anything like that.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:25.291
Statistically, bears shouldn't
be your biggest concern

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.926
while hiking in the forest.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.695
They don't normally attack people

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.263
for no apparent reason.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.965
Not unless they're startled...

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.166
or starving.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.534
If you do meet a bear

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.970
angry with you about the intrusion,

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.638
what should you do?

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.482
Well, the first thing to
know about bears -

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.985
they aren't all the same.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.254
Before choosing your survival strategy,

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:58.091
you'd be wise to identify the
bear running toward you.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.865
Color - medium-to-dark brown.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.835
Body length - 200 cm (6.5 feet).

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.371
Body features - round ears,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.772
long claws,

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:16.109
and a slight hump above the shoulder.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:19.312
If you go hiking in the
woods of Canada or Russia,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.548
be prepared for a date with a grizzly.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.551
Firearm?

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.985
Leave that thing at home.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.121
A study of bear-human conflicts

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.224
proved guns to be ineffective
when encountering a bear.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.327
But bear spray is a different story.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.929
Carry it in your front pocket.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.497
If a brown bear attacks you,

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.799
you'll only have a few seconds to fire.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.868
And don't run -

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.471
bears are fast, and they will catch you.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.840
Better to fall in the fetal position,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.342
protect your head, neck, and stomach.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.177
If a grizzly keeps attacking you,

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.445
play dead.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:55.548
Once the bear doesn't see
a threat in you, they'll leave.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:59.119
But first, they'll make sure
you're absolutely dead.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.688
It's better to stay down
for at least 20 minutes

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.557
after an attack, just in case.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.965
Color - from black to light blonde.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:15.301
Body length - 150 cm (5 feet).

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.771
Body features - straight facial profile,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:22.709
taller ears, and short claws.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:26.112
Black bears aren't as big or
as aggressive as grizzlies,

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.313
but they might attack you

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.882
if they feel threatened.

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:31.618
Whatever you do here,
don't play dead.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.453
These guys don't fall for that.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.255
Don't try to climb a tree either -

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:38.224
black bears are much
better climbers than you.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.895
Instead, get big, get loud,

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.597
and act as aggressively as you can.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.533
And don't forget about
your bear spray -

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.934
it works for all bears.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.708
Color - white.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:03:01.214
Body length - 210 - 330 cm (7-11 feet).

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.416
Body features - short tail,

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.885
and massive paws.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.588
If you find yourself alone in the Arctic,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.658
and the largest land carnivore
on Earth is running at you,

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:14.661
you've got yourself in big trouble.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:18.198
For a polar bear, you're
prey at first sight.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:21.100
You won't scare them
so easily with intimidation.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.871
Fighting a one-ton polar
bear - not a great idea either.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:28.308
Once again, bear
spray is your best bet.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.510
I mean, this is not an
ad for bear spray, but...

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.312
you should get some of this stuff.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.514
You're running into a lot of bears.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.216
If you do end up fighting the bear,

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.618
attack as if your life depends on it.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.086
Because it does.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.488
Try to aim for the nose or eyes.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.692
And watch out for those deadly paws.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.027
Ultimately, the best way to survive

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.563
is to avoid an encounter
in the first place.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:54.033
Lucky for you, most bears will
retreat when they hear you coming

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.569
before you even
know they're around.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.071
Still worried?

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.139
Let me just say that
you've got a higher chance

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.674
of dying from a wasp sting

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.710
than you do from a bear attack.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.345
Sometimes you can get hurt

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.080
when you're least expecting.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.181
Gotta have to stay tuned

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.516
for more survival how to's.

